AB  - Cloud computing offers us a wide range of services and facilities on a rental basis at a competitive price. But, due to the exponential increase in the number of cloud service buyers and service providers around the globe, it is challenging to decide which cloud service provider is suitable for desired service. The choice of the most efficient cloud service provider is a complex multi-criteria decision making (MCDM) problem. This paper provides a technique combining two MCDM approaches for a more robust, reliable, efficient, and fully consistent way to get a suitable cloud service provider. Our proposed work combines the Robust and Efficient Technique for Order of Preference by Similarity to Ideal Solution (RE-TOPSIS) and Best Only Method (BOM) to obtain the rank of participating cloud service providers. The validation of the proposed approach is performed with a use case to check the correctness of the method and found that the proposed method is more robust, efficient, and reliable than the existing state-of-the-works available in literature. It has been compared with integrated MCDM methods like BOM, BOM-TOPSIS, BWM-TOPSIS and AHP. It has been observed from the results that the proposed method performs better than AHP, BOM, BWM-TOPSIS and BOM-TOPSIS based service selection methods proposed by existing authors. © 2025 School of Science, DUTH. All rights reserved.
