AB  - With the development of global science and technology, computer network technology has been popularized and widely applied in every corner of people's life. At the same time, the field of software development has also been driven and developed rapidly. With the increasing complexity and difficulty of software project development, as well as the increasing needs of customers, software project management has gradually become a hot topic for scholars. In order to effectively prevent the risk of failure of software project development, the awareness and ability of software project risk management must be strengthened, and software project risk assessment is an important part of software risk management. At present, the research on software risk assessment in China is still lack of experience. Considering the fuzziness and uncertainty of the software project itself, this paper combines the Analytic Hierarchy Process (AHP) with the Fuzzy Comprehensive Evaluation (FCE) to determine the evaluation indexes, establishes the software risk evaluation system and evaluates the risk of the software project, which provides a new way to reduce the risk of the software project, enhance the ability of software to resist the risk, protect the basic interests of customers and improve the quality of software development, and has certain theoretical and practical value. © 2020 ACM.
