AB  - Software packages that meets the requirements of an organization should be appropriately investigated and evaluated. Picking up a wrong software package may adversely influence the business process and working function of an organization. Inappropriate software selection can turn out to be costly and it is a time-consuming decision-making process. This paper aims to provide a base for selecting the open source software packages based on analytic hierarchy process and technique for order preference similarity to ideal solution methodologies. In addition, the priority weights are generated and optimized by using teaching-learning based optimization approach. A well-organized algorithmic procedure is given in detail and a numerical example is examined to illustrate the validity and practicability of our proposed methodologies.  © 1988-2012 IEEE.
