AB  - Cloud Providers allows on-demand access and simple network connections to a shared resource pool. Because of the success and benefits of the use of Cloud Services, a range of business organizations are heading towards Cloud. The selection of the best Cloud Provider is a research topic, and this article addressing the same. Several other methods for addressing this problem and researchers suggested deploying Multi Criteria Decision-Making Models. Nevertheless, a significant number of works focused on quantitative QoS attributes and also the fuzziness involved in the QoS data was not handled in the existing works. So a framework for ranking and selection of Cloud Providers is proposed in this work. SMI attributes that are proposed by CSMIC and approved by ISO is used as the criteria for the ranking of the cloud providers in this research work. Fuzzy TOPSIS is the MCDM approach used to rank and select the best Cloud Provider in this proposed work. © 2020 IEEE.
