AB  - Online-CADCOM is a cloud platform that already helps engineers choose computer-aided design (CAD) tools by applying multi-criteria decision analysis (MCDA) to a structured database of tool profiles called 'passports'. This paper describes a new artificial-intelligence (AI) assistant that completes the design workflow. After the MCDA engine recommends the best primary tool, a GPT-4o-mini model suggests additional simulation, analysis, verification, and sourcing utilities, but only from the same internal database. A printed circuit board (PCB) design scenario shows how the AI assistant turns a single-tool suggestion into a full toolchain without exposing user schematics or inventing non-existent resources. Compared with the original MCDA-only module, the enhanced system covers more workflow stages, cuts manual search time, and preserves transparent, criteria-driven selection. Future work will extend the approach to other design domains and add learning-based weight adjustment. © 2025 University of Split, FESB.
