AB  - In recent years, with the rapid development of unmanned aerial vehicles (UAV) technology, easy-to-control, lowcost consumer and industrial UAVs have been widely used, accompanied by various 'black flying' phenomena that also pose a serious threat to public safety and national security, there is an urgent need for effective technical means to supervise UAV. Because of the limitations of the existing evaluation system of UAV detection and countermeasures strategies, this paper takes the application of various UAV detection and countermeasures strategies in the security conditions of major cities as the background, from preliminary targeting capability, public opinion guidance, detection accuracy, economic cost, effective range, time cost. By analyzing the specific situation model of security in various cities, the analytic hierarchy process is used to design the judgment matrix and the target matrix, and the APP Designer tool of MATLAB is used to design the visual program. Finally, a software platform for intelligent and visual UAV detection and countermeasure strategy evaluation system based on the Analytic Hierarchy Process (AHP) is built, which provides a theoretical reference for the detection and countermeasure of security UAVs in various cities. © 2024 IEEE.
