VL  - 23
C7  - 100747
DO  - 10.1016/j.nexus.2026.100747
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105044257572?origin=resultslist
AB  - Industry 5.0 (I5.0) can enhance Renewable Energy (RE) networks by improving optimization, resilience, and intelligence, but the lack of a systematic framework for prioritizing solutions limits this potential. This research prioritizes key I5.0 solutions in Iran's RE network using a comprehensive scenario-driven fuzzy decision-making framework. The Fuzzy Stepwise Weight Assessment Ratio Analysis (F-SWARA) technique determines factor significance, and the Fuzzy Measurement of Alternatives and Ranking according to COmpromise Solution (F-MARCOS) technique ranks the solutions. A full sensitivity analysis across all possible decision makers' weight scenarios (capturing diverse opinion dynamics) is conducted to validate robustness. Findings indicated the high importance of desirable investment volume, readiness of technical infrastructure for technology deployment, and technological flexibility in the implementation process, with values of 0.626, 0.610, and 0.572, respectively. The results revealed that the deployment of intelligent systems based on artificial intelligence and the Internet of Things, with the ability to predict demand and optimally manage operations, scientifically improves network efficiency. The implementation of intelligent resource management solutions through smart networks and advanced monitoring systems ensures operational and environmental sustainability. The development of technical infrastructure by creating high-speed communication networks and a centralized cloud platform acts as a basic prerequisite for the adoption of I5.0. The scenario-driven analysis confirms ranking robustness, supporting the framework's generalizability. © 2026 The Author(s).
