AB  - The paper substantiates the relevance of the problem of rational choice of information security tools for corporate digital solutions, especially for solutions with generative artificial intelligence (AI). The main milestones in the development of modern digital AI solutions are described, and arguments are given for choosing a methodology for determining the best set of protection tools for digital solutions with AI in a fuzzy environment. The methodology for evaluating and selecting a digital project in a multi-criteria formulation based on the fuzzy Sugeno integral is recommended to solve the problem of rational choice of information security tools for digital solutions with AI. The authors also proposed three vectors for the modern technological innovations in IT: digitalization, decentralization, and the increasing subjectivity of individual software models in digital solutions (as 'smartization'). A more detailed consideration of these vectors may further contribute to the development advanced methods for multi-criteria selection of cybersecurity tools to ensure the security of corporate IT infrastructures.  © 2026 IEEE.
