AB  - For software development teams, selecting appropriate agile practices is a difficult task due to differences in team structure, experience, and project context. This paper presents the design, development, and evaluation of an application that supports the selection of agile practices based on specific team characteristics. The application uses the SWARA (Stepwise Weight Assessment Ratio Analysis) multi-criteria decision-making method and filtering based on defined rules to recommend the most appropriate agile practices for each team. The research followed the Action Design Research (ADR) methodology, so the proposed application is grounded in theory and practice requirements. It collects team characteristics through a structured questionnaire, analyzes it using predefined rules and weighted criteria, and in the end recommends agile practices that most align with team context. Six development teams participated in the process of application evaluation. They assess the usability and effectiveness of a solution. The results of this research showed that application helps development teams to achieve better software quality and better refine their software development process to answer challenges in a dynamic agile environment. © 2026 The Authors.
