AB  - Industry 4.0 (I4.0) represents a new work paradigm, of which small- and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) are seeking to be part, but in general, they find it difficult to integrate. The objective of this paper is to select an ERP (Enterprise Resource Planning) system that will help an SME to start the digitalization process. The research focuses on the selection of an ERP system through a methodology called Systematic Help for ERP Acquisition (SHERPA) and a multi-criteria analysis called Weighted Aggregated Sum Product Assessment (WASPAS). In addition, entropy methods and the analytic hierarchy process (AHP) are used, integrating both objective and subjective criteria to determine their weights. The combination of these methods makes it possible to establish a systematic ERP selection tool. Through the conducted analysis in this study, it was decided to select Odoo as ERP system, in which some of the most influential factors were that it contemplates the business needs of the SME. © 2023, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG.
