AB  - Software defect prediction is an essential activity for software quality assurance. Various researchers have developed a large number of models for software defect prediction based on machine learning. Different models may have the varying capability for software defect prediction with respect to different conflicting accuracy measures. This paper aims to propose a Multi-Criteria Decision Making (MCDM) based approach for selecting the most appropriate machine learning technique for software defect prediction with respect to more than one accuracy measure. Because of the involvement of various accuracy measures, the problem of selecting an appropriate machine learning technique for software defect prediction can be modeled as a Multi-Criteria Decision Making (MCDM) problem. An experimental study was conducted using nine machine learning techniques, four performance measures and one MCDM method over three datasets to validate the proposed method. Experimental results of this study show that the proposed method can be applied as an efficient decision-making tool in software industries for choosing the most suitable machine learning technique for software defect prediction. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd 2023.
