AB  - The single-valued neutrosophic set (SVNS) regarded as a seductive tool for dealing uncertain and incomprehensible information. With this consideration, different from the most current distance-based method for order preference by TOPSIS technique, this approach offer correlation-based TOPSIS method for addressing the single-valued neutrosophic (SVN) multiple attribute decision making (MADM) problems. The weighted correlation coefficient of the SVN is presented in order to emphasize the importance of the factors. The concept index on the basis of correlation is further proposed for the installation of the focal framework of the TOPSIS, which is denoted the TOPSIS method on the base of SVN correlation and in this paper these approach is used for selection of software in enterprise. © 2021, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG.
