AB  - For a financial management major, which is practice-oriented, strengthening practical teaching and establishing a practice teaching quality evaluation system would help enhance students' professional ability and skills and ensure program quality at a high level. Hence, developing a practice teaching quality evaluation system that can effectively and objectively evaluate teaching quality and output is urgently needed. However, the university's teaching effectiveness evaluation of financial management majors requires multi-attribute group decision-making (MAGDM). Given that, recently, TODIM (TOmada de Decisão Interativa e Multicritério) and TOPSIS (Technique for Order Preference by Similarity to an Ideal Solution) have been applied to solve MAGDM, this study applies the interval neutrosophic number TODIM-TOPSIS method to solve MAGDM under the interval neutrosophic sets environment. This study conducts a case study of teaching effectiveness evaluation of financial management majors in universities to further substantiate the applicability of the proposed methodology. This article published as an Open Access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/) which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and production in any medium, provided the author of the original work and original publication source are properly credited.
